{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":65278,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"5d71a50a-b7ce-58d0-8bf8-16fc083289f7","total_cost_usd":0.5023369999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10085,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5924,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10085,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5924,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10085,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10085},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4327,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004417,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5924,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10085,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.49792,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:465d8368b0cdc3b167fd\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The input data contain exactly 24 data rows and 24 distinct site_id values (DS01 through DS24), each appearing on exactly one row, so no independent unit enters the cross-tabulation more than once. Verified by listing all site codes from line 2 through line 25 of the CSV.\",\"observed_value\":{\"data_rows\":24,\"unique_site_ids\":24,\"duplicated_site_ids\":0},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":2,\"quoted_text\":\"site_id,restoration_method,slack_area_m2,years_since_works,helleborine_present\\nDS01,inversion,1840,6,yes\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":25,\"end_line\":25,\"quoted_text\":\"DS24,stripping,1180,5,no\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow code explicitly enforces one row per independent unit: it raises a hard error if any site_id appears on more than one row before any statistics are computed, so a duplicated unit could not silently reach the Fisher test.\",\"observed_value\":\"ValueError raised on duplicated site_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":28,\"end_line\":30,\"quoted_text\":\"codes = [slack[\\\"site_id\\\"] for slack in slacks]\\n    if len(codes) != len(set(codes)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"site_id must appear on exactly one row\\\")\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description states each slack was surveyed and entered exactly once, ruling out repeated-measures structure hidden behind single rows, and confirms site_id values are unique.\",\"observed_value\":\"one survey per slack; site_id unique per row\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":14,\"end_line\":16,\"quoted_text\":\"The slacks are separated by dune ridges, were restored under separate\\ncontracts, and none of them was surveyed or entered twice, so each site yields a\\nsingle yes/no outcome and nothing more.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"- `site_id` - unique code for the slack, DS01 to DS24; appears on one row only.\"}]},{\"description\":\"Independent recomputation of the 2x2 table from the raw CSV gives inversion 9 present / 3 absent and stripping 3 present / 9 absent, odds ratio 9.00, and two-sided Fisher exact p = 2*(52901/2704156) = 0.0391, exactly matching the report; the reported result is therefore reproduced from unduplicated per-site rows.\",\"observed_value\":{\"table\":[[9,3],[3,9]],\"odds_ratio\":9,\"two_sided_p\":0.0391},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":19,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"| Deep topsoil inversion | 9 | 3 | 12 | 75.0% |\\n| Turf stripping | 3 | 9 | 12 | 25.0% |\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":26,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"- Fisher's exact test, two-sided: p = 0.0391\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The procedure used is of the row-independent type that this issue class targets: Fisher's exact test applied to rows treated as independent Bernoulli outcomes. This makes the analysis susceptible in principle if a unit were duplicated, but inspection of the data and code shows no duplication occurred, so this precondition alone does not demonstrate the issue.\",\"observed_value\":\"row-independent procedure present; no duplicated unit found\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":5,\"end_line\":7,\"quoted_text\":\"Each row of `data/input.csv` is one restored dune slack, walked once during the\\n2025 flowering season. No slack contributes more than one row, so the 24 rows\\nare 24 independent units and a row-independent test is appropriate.\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"from scipy.stats import fisher_exact\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) checking every site_id in data/input.csv for repeats: DS01-DS24 each appear exactly once across the 24 data rows; (2) looking for near-duplicate covariate rows (same method/area/age) that could indicate a re-entered site under a different code: all area values are distinct; (3) tracing the code path for any aggregation, merge, resampling, or loop that could feed a row into the 2x2 table more than once: cross_tabulate increments exactly one cell per row and read_slacks raises on duplicated codes; (4) recomputing the table, odds ratio (9.00), and two-sided Fisher p-value (0.0391) from the raw CSV, which matched the report exactly, confirming the reported result derives from one entry per independent unit. All attempts to exhibit a repeated independent-unit entry failed.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:465d8368b0cdc3b167fd","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The input data contain exactly 24 data rows and 24 distinct site_id values (DS01 through DS24), each appearing on exactly one row, so no independent unit enters the cross-tabulation more than once. Verified by listing all site codes from line 2 through line 25 of the CSV.","observed_value":{"data_rows":24,"unique_site_ids":24,"duplicated_site_ids":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"site_id,restoration_method,slack_area_m2,years_since_works,helleborine_present\nDS01,inversion,1840,6,yes"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"DS24,stripping,1180,5,no"}]},{"description":"The workflow code explicitly enforces one row per independent unit: it raises a hard error if any site_id appears on more than one row before any statistics are computed, so a duplicated unit could not silently reach the Fisher test.","observed_value":"ValueError raised on duplicated site_id","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":28,"end_line":30,"quoted_text":"codes = [slack[\"site_id\"] for slack in slacks]\n    if len(codes) != len(set(codes)):\n        raise ValueError(\"site_id must appear on exactly one row\")"}]},{"description":"The data description states each slack was surveyed and entered exactly once, ruling out repeated-measures structure hidden behind single rows, and confirms site_id values are unique.","observed_value":"one survey per slack; site_id unique per row","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":14,"end_line":16,"quoted_text":"The slacks are separated by dune ridges, were restored under separate\ncontracts, and none of them was surveyed or entered twice, so each site yields a\nsingle yes/no outcome and nothing more."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"- `site_id` - unique code for the slack, DS01 to DS24; appears on one row only."}]},{"description":"Independent recomputation of the 2x2 table from the raw CSV gives inversion 9 present / 3 absent and stripping 3 present / 9 absent, odds ratio 9.00, and two-sided Fisher exact p = 2*(52901/2704156) = 0.0391, exactly matching the report; the reported result is therefore reproduced from unduplicated per-site rows.","observed_value":{"table":[[9,3],[3,9]],"odds_ratio":9,"two_sided_p":0.0391},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":19,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"| Deep topsoil inversion | 9 | 3 | 12 | 75.0% |\n| Turf stripping | 3 | 9 | 12 | 25.0% |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":26,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"- Fisher's exact test, two-sided: p = 0.0391"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The procedure used is of the row-independent type that this issue class targets: Fisher's exact test applied to rows treated as independent Bernoulli outcomes. This makes the analysis susceptible in principle if a unit were duplicated, but inspection of the data and code shows no duplication occurred, so this precondition alone does not demonstrate the issue.","observed_value":"row-independent procedure present; no duplicated unit found","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"Each row of `data/input.csv` is one restored dune slack, walked once during the\n2025 flowering season. No slack contributes more than one row, so the 24 rows\nare 24 independent units and a row-independent test is appropriate."},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":12,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"from scipy.stats import fisher_exact"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) checking every site_id in data/input.csv for repeats: DS01-DS24 each appear exactly once across the 24 data rows; (2) looking for near-duplicate covariate rows (same method/area/age) that could indicate a re-entered site under a different code: all area values are distinct; (3) tracing the code path for any aggregation, merge, resampling, or loop that could feed a row into the 2x2 table more than once: cross_tabulate increments exactly one cell per row and read_slacks raises on duplicated codes; (4) recomputing the table, odds ratio (9.00), and two-sided Fisher p-value (0.0391) from the raw CSV, which matched the report exactly, confirming the reported result derives from one entry per independent unit. All attempts to exhibit a repeated independent-unit entry failed.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":37864,"ttft_stream_ms":1548,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"result","duration_ms":65803,"uuid":"de1800ad-66e7-4ead-aafc-62c70366f221"}
